[{:db/id "q-123154/selection/bb4e40eb75bdabc5d4b8fc8551e53b31faf62343d46997810fce12699577da64" :answer/id #uuid "32af4ca2-6e33-568a-8a99-0b7f7c3cdefd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\sqrt{7{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123154/selection/0d6588743927ecc4142d948cdd235d03b4a0af850664ab6918ad7c2aa223a5c0" :answer/id #uuid "dc581445-4802-5f45-9d5c-eae43fa48316" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123154/selection/32f0f3520cda9b27fad9aefcdc3794f1857ca8480c291a05e9168964c69cdd25" :answer/id #uuid "c7078e24-6cde-5d9d-97fd-f9570e28ddfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123154/selection/5bc85f7f8c585d4631cd2fc0ac728d535ecc128f9f7ab52a973c01aa5da5e23b" :answer/id #uuid "5e0a5dad-694e-58c3-902c-1c9bcc6afcf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\sqrt{7{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123154/selection/d5daff8b6a9fb94680ee4afa0fb3e6bbf4206749a21cc437aab2ad92ef8dba03" :answer/id #uuid "ce92fc80-d592-5c86-addd-8a922d230886" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+7}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123154/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "07e69715-995c-5d27-a00b-d8fb92832f5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123154/selection/5bc85f7f8c585d4631cd2fc0ac728d535ecc128f9f7ab52a973c01aa5da5e23b" :answer-field/choices ["q-123154/selection/bb4e40eb75bdabc5d4b8fc8551e53b31faf62343d46997810fce12699577da64" "q-123154/selection/0d6588743927ecc4142d948cdd235d03b4a0af850664ab6918ad7c2aa223a5c0" "q-123154/selection/32f0f3520cda9b27fad9aefcdc3794f1857ca8480c291a05e9168964c69cdd25" "q-123154/selection/5bc85f7f8c585d4631cd2fc0ac728d535ecc128f9f7ab52a973c01aa5da5e23b" "q-123154/selection/d5daff8b6a9fb94680ee4afa0fb3e6bbf4206749a21cc437aab2ad92ef8dba03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123154" :question/id #uuid "f9c98efc-0661-50b9-85fe-9ff3e5ffe73b" :question/math-academy-id "q-123154" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}-8{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the ellipse ${x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}=8,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $2\\sqrt{2}$ and $1,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7{sin}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-8{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-8(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =8{cos}^{2}⁡t-8{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =8({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}-8{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\sqrt{7{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\sqrt{7{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123154/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "440cb768-be67-5dd3-98c8-6a58f060245c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123154"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123146/selection/acb8430666aecd618dff11bb3bc60755a15cd9c04cd027385befcee4432974ec" :answer/id #uuid "5e194bcc-0351-5eb8-9153-ad266fe87766" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123146/selection/a3d442d53171fa1087623e6267a591feb4a5b38adc2e1dee5e85c91307c22b68" :answer/id #uuid "be3ce606-88cd-5a57-9605-c3efc9a626c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123146/selection/a27737dbc2ffc5c6552beecffaf2262c8e1d654f789c9cfbaf2d4681087d5604" :answer/id #uuid "f9e31b82-e9b3-5102-8d9f-efd7f5c17dca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123146/selection/dce32679c2b74e90690021dd5cc802e7a5a9bf202b311eab6cc5fadba0eaa026" :answer/id #uuid "5c69775c-6924-5bff-adf7-9cca7fb8ada1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123146/selection/76f642c1f90294e3d9561951cf97fe49eaedcdbe266c521e72679cd34f71656a" :answer/id #uuid "ad7f184b-092b-540c-98f6-a6e77f9bb051" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123146/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "361bbc11-5a63-5de1-8be9-0480c5d7a02a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123146/selection/76f642c1f90294e3d9561951cf97fe49eaedcdbe266c521e72679cd34f71656a" :answer-field/choices ["q-123146/selection/acb8430666aecd618dff11bb3bc60755a15cd9c04cd027385befcee4432974ec" "q-123146/selection/a3d442d53171fa1087623e6267a591feb4a5b38adc2e1dee5e85c91307c22b68" "q-123146/selection/a27737dbc2ffc5c6552beecffaf2262c8e1d654f789c9cfbaf2d4681087d5604" "q-123146/selection/dce32679c2b74e90690021dd5cc802e7a5a9bf202b311eab6cc5fadba0eaa026" "q-123146/selection/76f642c1f90294e3d9561951cf97fe49eaedcdbe266c521e72679cd34f71656a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123146" :question/id #uuid "ae604189-87b2-5cc4-80d1-9a191fe6507f" :question/math-academy-id "q-123146" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}2x\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}=64,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $4$ and $2,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12{sin}^{2}⁡t+4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12{sin}^{2}⁡t+4} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=2x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2x\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =16{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123146/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "440cb768-be67-5dd3-98c8-6a58f060245c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123146"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123150/selection/f86e986ba997d49a03722572be6d2d0983f749260996b046725c484d92108ea4" :answer/id #uuid "6fbd57b7-5043-536f-b1d7-3480e0035e61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\sqrt{6{cos}^{2}⁡t+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123150/selection/a68aea2c283ba7d445360e9a3718ca963092b0c261f20edfba0f80a81a282886" :answer/id #uuid "f99159f2-7b93-5906-8096-3965ac529545" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\sqrt{6{cos}^{2}⁡t+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123150/selection/ba86403dc100407dc2e9af4ce45a559d759a43ab1699131690853c4f71e7bc8b" :answer/id #uuid "a10a6cf1-9037-58dd-b916-e73c879694c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123150/selection/9896d4cb3f6ee4be8d85a0d5f6208b377c3b329ac2cd33a8d1d9baf9649541cc" :answer/id #uuid "3025af1a-4b43-5e42-8f80-154ebb492b27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123150/selection/b0bfe25bcd186fc9b0eaefb57a4db1463113f152b2155f25adc84e91fed87f6b" :answer/id #uuid "ab1073ba-f2a3-5a3d-9d98-4ca81ee72a53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\sqrt{6{cos}^{2}⁡t+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123150/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cbe9c63-6219-5e57-ae11-486a89471e72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123150/selection/a68aea2c283ba7d445360e9a3718ca963092b0c261f20edfba0f80a81a282886" :answer-field/choices ["q-123150/selection/f86e986ba997d49a03722572be6d2d0983f749260996b046725c484d92108ea4" "q-123150/selection/a68aea2c283ba7d445360e9a3718ca963092b0c261f20edfba0f80a81a282886" "q-123150/selection/ba86403dc100407dc2e9af4ce45a559d759a43ab1699131690853c4f71e7bc8b" "q-123150/selection/9896d4cb3f6ee4be8d85a0d5f6208b377c3b329ac2cd33a8d1d9baf9649541cc" "q-123150/selection/b0bfe25bcd186fc9b0eaefb57a4db1463113f152b2155f25adc84e91fed87f6b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123150" :question/id #uuid "5bcc7f53-1422-5f45-ba8f-525a5b3fcb14" :question/math-academy-id "q-123150" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}2xy\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the ellipse $8{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}=16,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $\\sqrt{2}$ and $2\\sqrt{2},$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡t+8{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6{cos}^{2}⁡t+2({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6{cos}^{2}⁡t+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=2xy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2xy\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\sqrt{6{cos}^{2}⁡t+2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\sqrt{6{cos}^{2}⁡t+2}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123150/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "440cb768-be67-5dd3-98c8-6a58f060245c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123150"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123153/selection/8b6bec9176d4cbb840e005afde74b772f7ef1bc8651a447dd4759fa096c82a9d" :answer/id #uuid "1f5815a3-713f-56d5-84d0-a638b2743796" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{6{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123153/selection/a79875ac38ed5c7c99f7679d75ac28478ac80bec90d2688cb07cd5c1bba63ef8" :answer/id #uuid "4ad24f67-b110-5702-b8c7-ec26f72204e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123153/selection/ee1e850e498263e7330e1715ed83c45bba6af1f30f00201d54137c4cfafab693" :answer/id #uuid "3d833881-bca7-5e07-9ced-41e6d9928097" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123153/selection/9ebebac318b04848d3ee2285c1ceba7f8d4d7ccc6b55dbc70850eb6854893161" :answer/id #uuid "901aabc6-59fa-5766-8d94-a185c27610cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{6{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123153/selection/bb8d99040ad8b8d62571cdb414c45064ac64dabcc1bda1e7d58ef8cb295c7801" :answer/id #uuid "81054924-9620-5f3b-a551-cb58053fd98c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{3{cos}^{2}⁡t+9}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123153/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "027666a7-fcce-572b-b78a-7a197be32417" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123153/selection/a79875ac38ed5c7c99f7679d75ac28478ac80bec90d2688cb07cd5c1bba63ef8" :answer-field/choices ["q-123153/selection/8b6bec9176d4cbb840e005afde74b772f7ef1bc8651a447dd4759fa096c82a9d" "q-123153/selection/a79875ac38ed5c7c99f7679d75ac28478ac80bec90d2688cb07cd5c1bba63ef8" "q-123153/selection/ee1e850e498263e7330e1715ed83c45bba6af1f30f00201d54137c4cfafab693" "q-123153/selection/9ebebac318b04848d3ee2285c1ceba7f8d4d7ccc6b55dbc70850eb6854893161" "q-123153/selection/bb8d99040ad8b8d62571cdb414c45064ac64dabcc1bda1e7d58ef8cb295c7801"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123153" :question/id #uuid "56d45ff5-8d46-5d91-ada0-7afe1d0328af" :question/math-academy-id "q-123153" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(3-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the ellipse $12{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=36,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $\\sqrt{3}$ and $2\\sqrt{3},$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+12{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+3({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=3-{x}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3-(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =3-3{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =3(1-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =3{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(3-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123153/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "440cb768-be67-5dd3-98c8-6a58f060245c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123153"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123145/selection/60d737ddbbf2d8ccd2fda157eead05c676252418dad326cd0890202109d70aee" :answer/id #uuid "490813e2-6e33-5992-896c-d18e143f4d94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123145/selection/c1242bac1f4a5e2c173259b983f839b964ae2e809d00dfa0625f7d841117df65" :answer/id #uuid "c65caf73-5c33-5769-a21a-8fdeb1c77635" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+48}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123145/selection/02f1528cdccb36175b444bec1744514cdf80f64a09d595cbee22cd51433fd0ad" :answer/id #uuid "b2bbb547-74c1-5756-857c-0b5a51e13fe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123145/selection/eb7f7f856582cd5d144a1a51ab1a2f2719818c7836745d6c50186ebb1548266f" :answer/id #uuid "30637a0b-74e6-518f-8f19-943519692066" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+48}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123145/selection/061f6ac9e236b2e0621aebffaae339f2a179ca60382947db7304b8fc2836b4b3" :answer/id #uuid "3835b51a-b1c0-50e3-9fc1-a91ea078569e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123145/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5ba98b8-bb2f-5eab-bd50-bbab73e0df84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123145/selection/02f1528cdccb36175b444bec1744514cdf80f64a09d595cbee22cd51433fd0ad" :answer-field/choices ["q-123145/selection/60d737ddbbf2d8ccd2fda157eead05c676252418dad326cd0890202109d70aee" "q-123145/selection/c1242bac1f4a5e2c173259b983f839b964ae2e809d00dfa0625f7d841117df65" "q-123145/selection/02f1528cdccb36175b444bec1744514cdf80f64a09d595cbee22cd51433fd0ad" "q-123145/selection/eb7f7f856582cd5d144a1a51ab1a2f2719818c7836745d6c50186ebb1548266f" "q-123145/selection/061f6ac9e236b2e0621aebffaae339f2a179ca60382947db7304b8fc2836b4b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123145" :question/id #uuid "02cef69c-cbb8-55b1-bcf6-b14618446fe6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123145" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}3y\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the ellipse $49{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=49,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $1$ and $7,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+49{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=3y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3(7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=21\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}3y\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }21\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =21{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{48{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123145/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "440cb768-be67-5dd3-98c8-6a58f060245c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123145"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123207/selection/b22cd9ceadd54d721c4740104951a0078e816438710e5173671af65c12e891cf" :answer/id #uuid "9c77de1e-15ba-524b-99b1-90bbf7157414" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123207/selection/3c1afb11c4cae89120b5f82e89679ee1d173cc3ede78eb461b50974d7ec4d369" :answer/id #uuid "d1febcdc-561f-5538-bc58-a57ab3c33c0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{3{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123207/selection/cc53dc3ff72d590d2703de886cc94f92446927764c2e81ba01f208e831d1c721" :answer/id #uuid "4062da8d-ef7b-52fc-9ace-4c21ad51daf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123207/selection/6a80323eaa6b6aeba10987daaa1b44ec3100083ae569a6c5567043a43c7c07c8" :answer/id #uuid "a0698b0c-ccf8-5184-8279-26540683e9d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{3{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123207/selection/6a95cdcde15b9c899e151f508754f78256500667c1b92c4a7e9d60a599d60357" :answer/id #uuid "ca297d11-44dd-5a10-90e5-7ff81cd186e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123207/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7d0eb7d-6b3b-5bff-bb9b-21799a4d50fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123207/selection/cc53dc3ff72d590d2703de886cc94f92446927764c2e81ba01f208e831d1c721" :answer-field/choices ["q-123207/selection/b22cd9ceadd54d721c4740104951a0078e816438710e5173671af65c12e891cf" "q-123207/selection/3c1afb11c4cae89120b5f82e89679ee1d173cc3ede78eb461b50974d7ec4d369" "q-123207/selection/cc53dc3ff72d590d2703de886cc94f92446927764c2e81ba01f208e831d1c721" "q-123207/selection/6a80323eaa6b6aeba10987daaa1b44ec3100083ae569a6c5567043a43c7c07c8" "q-123207/selection/6a95cdcde15b9c899e151f508754f78256500667c1b92c4a7e9d60a599d60357"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123207" :question/id #uuid "093d0403-9b58-520d-b909-bbab14fea8b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123207" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057969/assets/7fc64a261de4941b5ad35b8308b82b0f51c6b6bfbde177aafd793a0a0ac99da6.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the line integral ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is the quarter of the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=12,$ located in the second quadrant, shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $\\sqrt{3}$ and $2,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+3({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =3{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123207/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08dc697e-fd67-5ae0-889b-ea81c69e2277"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123207"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-122269"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057969/assets/3bf746cfb21805587a65c7beeac90e75464f630bab1fbf3453de69ca3e6639eb.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the line integral ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{4y}{x}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is the left half of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}=16,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $4$ and $1,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{15{sin}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{15{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{4y}{x},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{4y}{x} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{4y}{x}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\sqrt{15{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-123300/selection/79ed07cffd59feb7318ff9159eaec1faa620338ba71fbf844510714ce3edbb9b" :answer/id #uuid "f49794d5-760d-5492-a905-4c62062bce21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{11{cos}^{2}⁡t+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123300/selection/5a4337cea0a9b90c57601dc2ae1f26a68f47a850d4cdf58d820325d633be06cf" :answer/id #uuid "4a2eb3d5-810f-534d-ba09-02660c3482b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{11{cos}^{2}⁡t+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123300/selection/ba8ba030b55f031c67a8230dacd2ce94e92ec7fab4626603527c0d38b1b361c9" :answer/id #uuid "09b6d8af-f064-5864-9f44-f86a963b2440" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{36{cos}^{2}⁡t+11}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123300/selection/019aefc3ed480059ccd52dff48796e59713e28ed174dd4cab0c7349f38fe460a" :answer/id #uuid "2da8c64a-7c97-5f04-ab1d-3885a590e21d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{11{cos}^{2}⁡t+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123300/selection/2d7cd3eb1fe8cb68d6ee81d9242cc4f7ee77ed8d0efb29a20439ad0446641564" :answer/id #uuid "af7e39ce-3341-51a7-a480-7225a42da938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{36{cos}^{2}⁡t+11}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123300/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4415baa5-e63d-533c-ad25-a653091f46f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123300/selection/5a4337cea0a9b90c57601dc2ae1f26a68f47a850d4cdf58d820325d633be06cf" :answer-field/choices ["q-123300/selection/79ed07cffd59feb7318ff9159eaec1faa620338ba71fbf844510714ce3edbb9b" "q-123300/selection/5a4337cea0a9b90c57601dc2ae1f26a68f47a850d4cdf58d820325d633be06cf" "q-123300/selection/ba8ba030b55f031c67a8230dacd2ce94e92ec7fab4626603527c0d38b1b361c9" "q-123300/selection/019aefc3ed480059ccd52dff48796e59713e28ed174dd4cab0c7349f38fe460a" "q-123300/selection/2d7cd3eb1fe8cb68d6ee81d9242cc4f7ee77ed8d0efb29a20439ad0446641564"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123300" :question/id #uuid "2d67c9ae-1059-5bb6-951e-c7139ab21d55" :question/math-academy-id "q-123300" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057969/assets/34b4b349b8295ee6443a85f019f6bf5e7ea6c6aafe9109ac7935610e6aefcacf.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the line integral ${\\int }_{C}(25-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is three-quarters of the ellipse $36{x}^{2}+25{y}^{2}=900,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $5$ and $6,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{sin}^{2}⁡t+36{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11{cos}^{2}⁡t+25({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11{cos}^{2}⁡t+25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=25-{x}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =25-(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =25-25{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =25(1-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =25{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(25-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }25{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{11{cos}^{2}⁡t+25}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =25{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{11{cos}^{2}⁡t+25}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123300/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08dc697e-fd67-5ae0-889b-ea81c69e2277"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123300"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123302/selection/ca3f1f3e1a35581cfb8770c97d37bb846d205e4e2ec72d2eec6f599d32ad76b2" :answer/id #uuid "72f565e1-e4db-529b-a63e-0046f40df66f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123302/selection/347f81afac4e5e9ccfc2aad4d8e8b656694c9705d08db3c2c4eb22f42b82ba22" :answer/id #uuid "959cb165-6a9c-5b82-a50b-ce8cafc31eb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123302/selection/bbb9e6f84b6e8fe551d2d434accf05eb4986beaaef80b2576f7927d06744ab75" :answer/id #uuid "c93b437b-e2ab-5d65-86f2-db2ae6d8550c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123302/selection/8fb7784b53e38b8d3918ee736bb22e7cd2bcf54f251dd039feff2260420b69ac" :answer/id #uuid "a8ee88ae-11df-54a5-8f94-96a4728a78ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123302/selection/4ea3c60126c3d9690c7d58beb9710481364c0cd2eb0791414d24283aaa407368" :answer/id #uuid "34dd5337-0952-5f6c-9864-ca2512b27e9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123302/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c107bf22-1286-57e7-82e7-94848d947af8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123302/selection/8fb7784b53e38b8d3918ee736bb22e7cd2bcf54f251dd039feff2260420b69ac" :answer-field/choices ["q-123302/selection/ca3f1f3e1a35581cfb8770c97d37bb846d205e4e2ec72d2eec6f599d32ad76b2" "q-123302/selection/347f81afac4e5e9ccfc2aad4d8e8b656694c9705d08db3c2c4eb22f42b82ba22" "q-123302/selection/bbb9e6f84b6e8fe551d2d434accf05eb4986beaaef80b2576f7927d06744ab75" "q-123302/selection/8fb7784b53e38b8d3918ee736bb22e7cd2bcf54f251dd039feff2260420b69ac" "q-123302/selection/4ea3c60126c3d9690c7d58beb9710481364c0cd2eb0791414d24283aaa407368"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123302" :question/id #uuid "35879d4d-b93c-502a-9dd1-7fe3a9e004c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-123302" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057969/assets/59296f25e2060b05f95ddc69f560e987f933d69f8966c1859ea0cd54bbb80175.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the line integral ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{y}{2x}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is three-quarters of the ellipse $2{x}^{2}+18{y}^{2}=36,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(3\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $3\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{2},$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,-\\pi \\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+2({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{2x},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{2(3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{y}{2x}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+2}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123302/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08dc697e-fd67-5ae0-889b-ea81c69e2277"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123302"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123304/selection/2c6058a0296e27149ac03c88c0a0e77c6b76c67d3767dd11f7e9c7c4a7224d23" :answer/id #uuid "bafc6001-8beb-5941-b60d-48ef35545377" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123304/selection/3061e4119352f2cd3d749791164e0f6b8ed3ceef0b4515194a1ec9248121ff4f" :answer/id #uuid "66c21f98-0863-5cbe-bba1-ddc0c4688a3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123304/selection/47f85ecdf3992e7966ed737469eccdaa8e1c9874d5521aa01c3dd1e413b8b1af" :answer/id #uuid "e649283c-1f89-5d38-89bf-1e681c810389" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123304/selection/dde0a40089bdb77caa3571fd36d65fcac0eae1ca981a4cb3d52d296df749da54" :answer/id #uuid "26b12f5a-4995-5ebd-822a-c90d973deb34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123304/selection/a7897581bd0b99dfe072a89bd2c7691ebd0ef00a3049338e3042ccc3e8cbb944" :answer/id #uuid "fbeccb36-6096-5cf9-a644-72ed7892a8cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123304/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "10102064-8838-50dc-a90c-026e69d4666e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123304/selection/3061e4119352f2cd3d749791164e0f6b8ed3ceef0b4515194a1ec9248121ff4f" :answer-field/choices ["q-123304/selection/2c6058a0296e27149ac03c88c0a0e77c6b76c67d3767dd11f7e9c7c4a7224d23" "q-123304/selection/3061e4119352f2cd3d749791164e0f6b8ed3ceef0b4515194a1ec9248121ff4f" "q-123304/selection/47f85ecdf3992e7966ed737469eccdaa8e1c9874d5521aa01c3dd1e413b8b1af" "q-123304/selection/dde0a40089bdb77caa3571fd36d65fcac0eae1ca981a4cb3d52d296df749da54" "q-123304/selection/a7897581bd0b99dfe072a89bd2c7691ebd0ef00a3049338e3042ccc3e8cbb944"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123304" :question/id #uuid "62367725-c26e-50a6-8496-8a057a37c1b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123304" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057969/assets/1e09fa361aca812f22d9d28430a8584e069c0eb9a2aa90f5e665d892dddd378f.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the line integral ${\\int }_{C}(5-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is three-quarters of the ellipse $5{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $1$ and $\\sqrt{5},$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+5{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=5-{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =5-(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =5-5{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =5(1-{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =5{cos}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(5-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}5{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123304/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08dc697e-fd67-5ae0-889b-ea81c69e2277"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123304"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123181/selection/879a225aaf1b8272157c33247ace982b7e338d5701ba0d4d6c31dd38d4da6784" :answer/id #uuid "94aa24ba-bf34-5b96-a5c9-da3218ab0cde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123181/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" :answer/id #uuid "da0c3949-432f-5b56-a21a-338209970dd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123181/selection/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer/id #uuid "75e6e018-808b-5e84-a61d-0d53daf222f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123181/selection/5d75fc115d122bcf89c08ce3361f5bf132566cb78a3191c8592f2028be7e68b0" :answer/id #uuid "5a5bd2ca-0882-5bc5-8e88-96c70f588f25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123181/selection/bc8ddfe9b0ae9ecd586464d3b828bfdd8a405438588d3184601cef690877fd8c" :answer/id #uuid "6d6c8f8e-e476-5a98-bbb8-643a5728a4ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-34" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123181/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "01a94afb-c18f-5df6-ac71-1817c0b3597d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123181/selection/5d75fc115d122bcf89c08ce3361f5bf132566cb78a3191c8592f2028be7e68b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-123181/selection/879a225aaf1b8272157c33247ace982b7e338d5701ba0d4d6c31dd38d4da6784" "q-123181/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" "q-123181/selection/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" "q-123181/selection/5d75fc115d122bcf89c08ce3361f5bf132566cb78a3191c8592f2028be7e68b0" "q-123181/selection/bc8ddfe9b0ae9ecd586464d3b828bfdd8a405438588d3184601cef690877fd8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123181" :question/id #uuid "45c2d2f4-3056-5d3b-a93e-41019ae1d85a" :question/math-academy-id "q-123181" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057969/assets/570b00c901daedddc9fe05855e2df5fb2c24158320544b955bda651210d9f803.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}16xy\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is the quarter of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=9$  traversed from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(-3,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $3$ and $1,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{sin}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+8{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=16xy$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =16\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t=48\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}16xy\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }48\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\sqrt{1+8{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =48{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{1+8{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=1+8{sin}^{2}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}48{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{1+8{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{9}^{1}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{9}^{1} \\\\  & =2({1}^{3/2}-{9}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =2(1-27) \\\\  & =-52\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-123181/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ed80030-2c39-5b66-a3c5-fb1a8428a780"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123181"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123281/selection/c899b66a44e06a12a94d3251fe6a8cb72bcfd9e0848a48e82c42daae83565fc2" :answer/id #uuid "0fd240a2-0ce4-5c23-9121-c14de5295a83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{128}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123281/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" :answer/id #uuid "1f362edb-6f6e-55d0-8206-093517d8d4d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123281/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "58950fc5-1581-5b4b-af46-7b51907cce5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123281/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "0ec5f5ba-b824-5cd1-a5ae-0399985a98b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123281/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "5d964518-4e61-59aa-831e-4a7eb50521b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123281/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fbe463c-47aa-5a59-8313-e878240370b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123281/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-123281/selection/c899b66a44e06a12a94d3251fe6a8cb72bcfd9e0848a48e82c42daae83565fc2" "q-123281/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" "q-123281/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-123281/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-123281/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123281" :question/id #uuid "5d9815d1-8f4e-574f-9bc1-e49b807f4188" :question/math-academy-id "q-123281" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=9xy$ along the ellipse $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=16,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $4$ and $\\frac{4}{3},$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+\\frac{16}{9}{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{8{sin}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{8{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=9xy$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =9\\cdot 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=48\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}9xy\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }48\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{8{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =64{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{8{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=8{sin}^{2}⁡t+1,$ $\\text{d}u=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{8{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t & =4{\\int }_{1}^{1}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{1} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123281/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ed80030-2c39-5b66-a3c5-fb1a8428a780"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123281"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123206/selection/b0b7d51233dfed21f90a3063acd0953ec76f008efcb7aebaf262a75a9f84a072" :answer/id #uuid "defa6bff-5914-5b7b-9ced-c9a00d33d98e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-148" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123206/selection/9a2c0f137f7fb9298cf3554da60658106395d030c4c60175330a7e0c456976f5" :answer/id #uuid "76e1bcfe-4d8d-5e9f-8df5-2697eab7f8cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123206/selection/25b335c1798b7b6a4cb13a35c15bf802d740cecd154b47b5e805a756e83b1528" :answer/id #uuid "b1afae64-49e1-5b61-bda5-9e52dd170301" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123206/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer/id #uuid "53737810-7c85-53a3-9e82-0004c44e4b2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123206/selection/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326" :answer/id #uuid "dcfa4cfb-d6a6-528d-a544-3eb5b28c8a69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "84" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123206/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f379e703-dbba-55cb-a280-afe8dc98da21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123206/selection/b0b7d51233dfed21f90a3063acd0953ec76f008efcb7aebaf262a75a9f84a072" :answer-field/choices ["q-123206/selection/b0b7d51233dfed21f90a3063acd0953ec76f008efcb7aebaf262a75a9f84a072" "q-123206/selection/9a2c0f137f7fb9298cf3554da60658106395d030c4c60175330a7e0c456976f5" "q-123206/selection/25b335c1798b7b6a4cb13a35c15bf802d740cecd154b47b5e805a756e83b1528" "q-123206/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" "q-123206/selection/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123206" :question/id #uuid "6c4aca3e-8652-5cdf-a70a-38e9f772a042" :question/math-academy-id "q-123206" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057969/assets/f1a234c8ec4ac3e2dcc4c2bfd2232c006179a3ca7597c05afbb4243435eca387.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}7xy\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is the quarter of the ellipse $9{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}=144$  traversed from the point $(0,-3)$ to the point $(4,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $3$ and $4,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7{sin}^{2}⁡t+(9{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+7{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=7xy$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =7\\cdot 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=84\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}7xy\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }84\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\sqrt{9+7{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =84{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{9+7{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=9+7{sin}^{2}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=14\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}84{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{9+7{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & =6{\\int }_{16}^{9}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{16}^{9} \\\\  & =4({9}^{3/2}-{16}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =4(27-64) \\\\  & =-148\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-123206/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ed80030-2c39-5b66-a3c5-fb1a8428a780"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123206"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123211/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "809245f3-e504-5203-a8cd-a5e2eacc5a87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123211/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce" :answer/id #uuid "c23ec94a-8606-5a1b-9cb0-e1c47dd38b45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123211/selection/f6700a5dffca4dc98ca5d8c7931e83f63ea427332b6fb1c1a620136bbafd5e94" :answer/id #uuid "051ab59a-8fb9-5f84-a41f-feb0cdee58f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123211/selection/c8cc0193c097b7d38e4091db7b8ea0b55b90f570b6dfeef91f6d5caca670d84e" :answer/id #uuid "24eb9efb-7323-50ba-a5ed-ab3e17befe3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123211/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "4ecf58f6-ac91-57f9-8d68-86ab237014b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123211/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f73b2a7-37e1-5db3-9dd3-5ee2dba574dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123211/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-123211/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-123211/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce" "q-123211/selection/f6700a5dffca4dc98ca5d8c7931e83f63ea427332b6fb1c1a620136bbafd5e94" "q-123211/selection/c8cc0193c097b7d38e4091db7b8ea0b55b90f570b6dfeef91f6d5caca670d84e" "q-123211/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123211" :question/id #uuid "ee274e18-3558-59cd-ad71-ce2d32a8f69d" :question/math-academy-id "q-123211" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=xy(3+2{y}^{2})$ along the ellipse $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=9,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $3$ and $\\sqrt{3},$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+3{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6{sin}^{2}⁡t+3({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3+6{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=xy(3+2{y}^{2})$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (3+2(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2})=3\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,(3+6{sin}^{2}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}xy(3+2{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(3+6{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\cdot \\sqrt{3+6{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{(3+6{sin}^{2}⁡t)}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=3+6{sin}^{2}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{(3+6{sin}^{2}⁡t)}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}{\\int }_{3}^{3}{u}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}{|}_{3}^{3} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123211/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ed80030-2c39-5b66-a3c5-fb1a8428a780"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123211"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123205/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "8fd1a98e-e372-5645-bc65-16a9e57bb1dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123205/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "d750e38d-3877-5583-9a10-87d2c301a7f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123205/selection/181d1f839d214e5807f4235aba03fc371467f433c702fbf48b29ccfdaa41b68d" :answer/id #uuid "acef585d-939b-5cff-9f31-c1a740a93ed6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123205/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "3c2ee34b-cb77-5931-9f08-a43f2129124c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123205/selection/5048951f5787df5b4e66c729d300d473c2356e9097b4f01b088bd5252ede9c54" :answer/id #uuid "dab4cdb5-d816-5082-8e38-0096dcbf2e38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123205/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e711804e-1358-50e9-8d2f-56b62f5ebef1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123205/selection/5048951f5787df5b4e66c729d300d473c2356e9097b4f01b088bd5252ede9c54" :answer-field/choices ["q-123205/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" "q-123205/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-123205/selection/181d1f839d214e5807f4235aba03fc371467f433c702fbf48b29ccfdaa41b68d" "q-123205/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-123205/selection/5048951f5787df5b4e66c729d300d473c2356e9097b4f01b088bd5252ede9c54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123205" :question/id #uuid "946964ae-09ce-57af-9a90-4baf950824d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-123205" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057969/assets/f3776aa331fba6b94bf24ebe254010d9b5954ba2a8edb6635be658e38bbc4039.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}8xy\\sqrt{1+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is the quarter of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}=5$  traversed from the point $(\\sqrt{5},0)$ to the point $(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $\\sqrt{5}$ and $1,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=8xy\\sqrt{1+4{y}^{2}}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =8\\cdot \\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\sqrt{1+4{sin}^{2}⁡t}=8\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+4{sin}^{2}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}8xy\\sqrt{1+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}8\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+4{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+4{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(1+4{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=1+4{sin}^{2}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(1+4{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{1}^{5}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}{|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}({5}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}(25-1) \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-123205/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ed80030-2c39-5b66-a3c5-fb1a8428a780"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123205"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9460"] :question/problem "What expression is equivalent to $\\displaystyle \\int_\\limits{C} \\dfrac{x}{y} \\: \\textrm{d}s,$ where $C$ is the ellipse $x^2 + 16y^2 = 16,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{4^2} + \\dfrac{y^2}{1^2} = 1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $4$ and $1,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\left\\langle 4\\cos{t}, \\: \\sin{t} \\right\\rangle, \\qquad 0 \\le t \\lt 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{15{sin}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{15{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{x}{y},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=4\\operatorname{cot}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\sqrt{15{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\sqrt{15{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9488"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057969/assets/71df4fc7bd52fe5dd97c7e01502dec2ad68ae31fdf224cccd812c6b7318c70b7.png)\n\nFind, as a definite integral, an expression for the line integral of the function $\\displaystyle\\int_\\limits{C} 2xy \\:\\textrm{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is the right half of the ellipse $9x^2 + 4y^2 = 36,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{2^2} + \\dfrac{y^2}{3^2} = 1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $2$ and $3,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\left\\langle 2\\cos{t}, \\: 3\\sin{t} \\right\\rangle, \\qquad -\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\le t \\le \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{cos}^{2}⁡t+4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = 2xy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2xy\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{5{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =12{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{5{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9439"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057969/assets/fda8bfb0533b86dc4050d1b8e309e332996b26263b1052d3e251bf0a5c98e816.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral $\\displaystyle\\int_\\limits{C}12xy\\:\\textrm{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is the quarter-ellipse $4x^2+y^2=4$ traversed from the point $(0,2)$ to the point $(-1,0),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\nx^2 + \\dfrac{y^2}{2^2}  = 1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $1$ and $2,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\big\\langle \\cos{t}, \\: 2\\sin{t} \\big\\rangle, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\le t \\le \\pi.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3{cos}^{2}⁡t+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+3{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = 12xy$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =12\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=24\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}12xy\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }24\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\sqrt{1+3{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =24{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{1+3{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=1+3\\cos^2 {t},$ $\\textrm d u=-6\\sin t\\cos \n t\\,\\textrm d t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{1+3{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & =-4{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}({4}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}(8-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{56}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
